WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.720
Malcolm In The Middle star Frankie&nbsp;
Muniz grew up in front of audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.920
from his hit show to his starring roles in&nbsp;
Agent Cody Banks and Big Fat Liar. He's kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.040
a low profile since, so here's what Muniz has been&nbsp;
up to since saying goodbye to playing Malcolm.
 

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.600
After the final episode of Malcolm&nbsp;
in the Middle aired in 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.400
fans were eager to find out what Muniz would&nbsp;
do next, but he needed a change of pace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.400
Even before going to Hollywood, Muniz&nbsp;
was active in theater, which was how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.360
he eventually transitioned into appearing in&nbsp;
commercials and landing his first film roles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.720
Muniz had been playing Malcolm for six years, and&nbsp;
he was ready for some time away from the camera.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.880
Muniz once said that by the time his&nbsp;
run as Malcolm was over, he had quote -

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.040
"done little else but work for 12 years."

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.840
That kind of schedule would be difficult&nbsp;
enough for an adult actor to handle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.560
let alone a child actor. He didn't leave&nbsp;
Hollywood altogether, but significantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.440
cut back on his schedule, mostly making&nbsp;
one-off appearances on TV shows or movies.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:07.680
After shooting Agent Cody Banks 2 in 2004, Muniz&nbsp;
began to think about landing more mature roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.120
but he admitted that dealing with&nbsp;
the transition was challenging.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.880
In an interview with About, the actor commented&nbsp;
that he assumed that upon becoming a legal adult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.360
he'd begin getting more mature roles,&nbsp;
but that wasn't the case, saying -

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.920
"I haven't been scared but I've really been&nbsp;
thinking about it a lot, that I really have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.480
do something at this point right now to break the&nbsp;
mold […] I really need to do something different."

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.360
But Muniz struggled to navigate this phase&nbsp;
in his career, after becoming so well known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.600
for his past characters that he wasn't taken&nbsp;
seriously in other roles. For instance, in 2007,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:47.920
he switched gears with a role in the rom-com My&nbsp;
Sexiest Year, which received middling reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.586
and in 2008, he appeared in Extreme&nbsp;
Movie, which was panned by critics.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.560
Eventually, Muniz decided to take up a new&nbsp;
passion that surprised some of his fans.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:06.080
In 2001, he drove the pace car in the Toyota 500,&nbsp;
and in 2004, he won the Toyota Pro-Celebrity Race.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:12.720
However, he knew that there was no way he'd be&nbsp;
able to balance both acting and racing. In 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.581
he decided to simply go on hiatus from&nbsp;
acting for a while, telling BBC News -

00:02:17.581 --> 00:02:22.960
"I want to want to act and, right now, I want&nbsp;
to race. You can't really juggle both because,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.760
if you do, you just don't&nbsp;
get enough time in the car."

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:31.040
This wasn't an impulsive decision on Muniz's&nbsp;
part. He spent plenty of time training to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.080
get behind the wheel, and he impressed his&nbsp;
instructors. He competed with Jensen MotorSport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.120
and his solid performance&nbsp;
in pre-season testing earned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.840
praise from team boss Eric Jensen.&nbsp;
Muniz raced for several years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.800
closing out his racing career with another showing&nbsp;
at the Toyota Pro-Celebrity Race in 2011.
 

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.960
While racing, Muniz got&nbsp;
into an accident and became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.240
seriously injured, saying&nbsp;
on Dancing With the Stars -

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.080
"I had a crash and broke my back&nbsp;
and injured my hands and ribs."

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:05.200
It took him quite a while to recover, and he&nbsp;
still feels the effects of these injuries today.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:09.520
He admitted that he and his dance partner,&nbsp;
Witney Carson, ended up talking about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.000
injuries all the time during rehearsals&nbsp;
because he felt like he had quote -

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.640
"the creaky, old body of a 71-year-old."

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.360
He didn't let his past injuries hold him back&nbsp;
from pursuing other exciting opportunities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.640
and he still considers himself&nbsp;
an active, athletic person.
 
 

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.480
At the age of seven, Muniz got his first&nbsp;
concussion while playing soccer, and since then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.760
he has suffered eight more. Later in life, he&nbsp;
began dealing with frightening mini-strokes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.800
In fact, Muniz says that he had visited&nbsp;
the emergency room on at least 15 different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.600
occasions because of these adverse health&nbsp;
events. The fact that he survived his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:51.040
mini-stroke was nothing if not miraculous: He&nbsp;
realized that something was wrong while he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:56.000
riding his motorcycle, and while losing his&nbsp;
vision, he somehow made it home to his family.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.640
"I kinda lost all peripheral vision,&nbsp;
and like started feeling like I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.301
losing my balance and uh, just started&nbsp;
feeling really really uncomfortable."

00:04:04.754 --> 00:04:10.080
To this day, Muniz has no clear answers as&nbsp;
to why he has suffered from mini-strokes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.800
He's always been very focused on living a&nbsp;
healthy lifestyle, telling Entertainment Weekly -

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.560
"I'm 31, I've never sipped alcohol, I've never&nbsp;
touched a drug or taken a drag of a cigarette.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.720
The only thing I've felt was stress.&nbsp;
I'm a high-strung person. I just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.000
to always be moving. I'm not good at relaxing." 
 
 

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.560
For the most part, Muniz hasn't endured&nbsp;
long-term complications from experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.920
mini-strokes. But he has dealt with one&nbsp;
setback: memory loss. Muniz admits that today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.856
he doesn't remember much of his time&nbsp;
working on Malcolm in the Middle.

00:04:41.856 --> 00:04:45.520
But Muniz says that for the most part,&nbsp;
his memory loss doesn't bother him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.080
Although dealing with these&nbsp;
health issues can be difficult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.440
he chooses to stay focused on the positives.&nbsp;
His wife, Paige Price, even helps him keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:58.506
track of things they've done together by writing&nbsp;
them down in a journal. As Muniz told People -

00:04:58.506 --> 00:05:02.240
"I only know what it's like to be&nbsp;
me and if I don't let it bother me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.360
I just try to live the most&nbsp;
fulfilling, best life I can.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.880
I really try to take advantage of my&nbsp;
time. And I've got a lot in my life."
 

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:14.320
Muniz has a wide variety of interests.&nbsp;
Ian addition to acting and racing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:18.800
he's also passionate about music. He&nbsp;
began playing the drums when he was 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.520
and he always enjoyed it as a hobby and&nbsp;
a momentary reprieve from the spotlight.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.560
"I'm the drummer you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.280
no one looks at the drummer. You know&nbsp;
what I mean? You got the front man -"

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:31.320
"Sorry man, no-nobody,&nbsp;
nobody looks at the drummer."

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.320
"Sorry."

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:38.400
In 2012, Muniz decided to put his racing career&nbsp;
on hold in order to pursue music professionally.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.440
He joined the band You Hang Up as a drummer&nbsp;
when they were unsigned. It all started with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:49.520
random message from Aaron Brown, the band's lead&nbsp;
vocalist and guitarist, as Muniz told PennLive -

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.680
"Aaron called and asked if I'd be interested&nbsp;
in jamming with them, since he knew I played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.080
drums. I was like, 'I don't want to jam&nbsp;
with you guys, I want to be in the band!'"

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:04.160
Later, Muniz went on to play drums with the&nbsp;
band Kingsfoil and in 2017, he switched gears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.120
and began managing the band Astro Lasso,&nbsp;
taking them on tour with We the Kings.
 
 

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.680
Although Muniz has taken long&nbsp;
stretches of time away from acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.720
he never walked away from the industry. Throughout&nbsp;
the years since Malcolm in the Middle ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:24.240
Muniz has occasionally done guest spots on TV&nbsp;
shows and appeared in supporting roles in movies.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:30.160
Unfortunately for Muniz, most of his films&nbsp;
have not gotten glowing reviews. In 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.960
he appeared in the family flick Another Day&nbsp;
in Paradise, which told the story of two girls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:40.960
helping their widowed father accept their mother's&nbsp;
death. In 2018, Muniz went in a new direction when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:46.240
he starred in the horror film The Black String.&nbsp;
Interestingly enough, critics weren't crazy about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:52.400
the film, but Muniz's performance did earn some&nbsp;
praise with critic Brittany Witherspoon writing -

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:56.400
"Elevating this script from a derivative&nbsp;
and simple one is no easy task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.320
but Muniz does it effortlessly." 
 

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:04.800
Muniz moved to Arizona because he was ready to&nbsp;
get away from Los Angeles, telling PennLive -

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.840
"I always say moving out of LA and moving&nbsp;
to Phoenix, I feel, saved my life."

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:13.200
Later, Muniz settled down in&nbsp;
Scottsdale with his partner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:20.240
Paige Price, whom he married in 2019. The couple&nbsp;
loved the area's unique charm and Old West vibes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.480
However, he says that new developments&nbsp;
in the city have made him a bit concerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:28.480
for Scottsdale's future, lamenting&nbsp;
in an interview with AZ Central -

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:33.920
"It's becoming like a little bit of a mini LA.&nbsp;
Not that I want to get into an LA bash-fest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.960
but I moved here because I love what&nbsp;
it has here. [...] I hope it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.200
grow too big where you lose some of that charm."
 

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.560
Muniz and Price bought Outrageous&nbsp;
Olive Oils &amp; Vinegars in Scottsdale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.200
Arizona, and became small business owners.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.626
"My fiance and I were looking&nbsp;
to do something together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.626 --> 00:07:53.920
and we found this little - this store and this&nbsp;
brand and we loved it and we took it over."

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.360
And Muniz didn't simply hire&nbsp;
people to run the store for him;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.880
he took a very hands-on approach,&nbsp;
with the couple bottling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:06.480
labeling, and sealing everything themselves. As&nbsp;
he explained in an interview with AZ Central -

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:11.120
"It's a lot of work, but it's really rewarding&nbsp;
when people come in and rave about the product."

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:16.560
Muniz and Price were genuinely proud of the olive&nbsp;
oils and other products they put on the shelves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:22.400
before selling the shop in 2020. 
 
 
In September 2020, Muniz and Price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:27.120
excitedly announced that they were going to&nbsp;
become parents. The couple revealed to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:33.040
fans that they would be welcoming a baby boy into&nbsp;
their family. In the announcement Muniz said -

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:38.160
"While we still believe it's the little moments in&nbsp;
between the big ones that make you feel happiest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.440
nothing quite compares to hearing&nbsp;
your little one's heartbeat."

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:45.680
From that moment, Muniz's focus&nbsp;
in life completely shifted:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.960
he immediately started suggesting baby names and&nbsp;
wondering what their child's future would be like.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:57.600
The couple welcomed their son Mauz on March&nbsp;
22nd, 2021, and now it looks like Muniz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.760
will be focused on spending lots of time&nbsp;
with his family and enjoying fatherhood.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.120
Fans of Muniz will be happy to hear that&nbsp;
despite stepping away from Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.320
he has no intentions of retiring from&nbsp;
acting altogether. Early in 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:18.160
Muniz had a guest role as Corey Harris on the&nbsp;
comedic crime drama The Rookie. He's also set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:25.200
to play a deputy in the Western film Hot Bath an'&nbsp;
a Stiff Drink 2, and has a role in Road to Capri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:30.560
a comedy film about two brothers who only discover&nbsp;
that they're related after their father's death.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.720
While Muniz might never commit as&nbsp;
much time to acting as he once did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.920
he'll likely stick around in&nbsp;
Hollywood for years to come.

